[37.786559, "o", "site_packages = '/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages'\r\n\r\nwith zipfile.ZipFile(wheel) as zf:\r\n    for name in zf.namelist():\r\n        # Skip the dist-info directory (already exists)\r\n        if name.startswith('pip-24.3.1.dist-info/'):\r\n            continue\r\n        dest = os.path.join(site_packages, name)\r\n        if name.endswith('/'):\r\n            os.makedirs(dest, exist_ok=True)\r\n        else:\r\n            os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(dest), exist_ok=True)\r\n            with zf.open(name) as src, open(dest, 'wb') as dst:\r\n                dst.write(src.read())\r\n            print(f'Extracted: {name}')\r\n\r\nprint('Done.')\r\n\" 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash python3 -c \" import zipfile, os, shutil wheel = '/usr/local/lib/python…\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 12 tool call(s) so far\r\n  │ Now let me verify pip works:\r\n[approval] bash: pip3 --version 2>&1 && python3 -m pip --version 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash pip3 --version 2>&1 && python3 -m pip --version 2>&1\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6"]
[37.786595, "o", "-35b — 13 tool call(s) so far\r\n  │ Let me do a quick sanity check that installing a package actually works:\r\n[approval] bash: pip3 install --dry-run requests 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash pip3 install --dry-run requests 2>&1\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 14 tool call(s) so far\r\nPip is fully restored and working.\r\n\r\n**What was wrong:** The `pip` Python package directory was missing from `/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/`. Only the `pip-24.3.1.dist-info` metadata folder remained — the actual `pip/` source code and all its vendored dependencies had been deleted. The `pip3` entry point script was intact but couldn't `import pip`, so it crashed with `ModuleNotFoundError`.\r\n\r\n**What I did:** Extracted the bundled pip wheel (`pip-24.3.1-py3-none-any.whl`) from `/usr/local/lib/python3.13/ensurepip/_bundled/` back into site-packages, restoring the full `pip/` package and all its `_vendor/` dependencies.\r\n\r\n**Verification:** Both `pip3 --version` and `python3 -m pip --version` report `pip 24"]
[37.786603, "o", ".3.1`, and a dry-run install of `requests` resolves all dependencies correctly.\r\n\r\n[refusal] role=implementor model=qwen3.6-35b tools=14 surface=1214d171567f\r\n"]
